# Ephemeral implementation plans

`docs/superpowers/plans/` may hold a **local** working plan while implementing. Treat it as scratch, not product history.

## Do

- Write plans locally when using the writing-plans / executing-plans flow
- Keep the plan untracked (`git status` should not show it staged)
- **Delete the plan file** once the feature is implemented (or the PR is open and you no longer need the checklist)
- Put durable decisions in `docs/superpowers/specs/` and `docs/adr/` instead

## Don't

- Never `git add` or commit a new plan under `docs/superpowers/plans/`
- Never force-add a plan around `.gitignore`
- Do not treat plans as the long-term source of truth (specs/ADRs are)

Historical plans already on `main` stay; this rule applies to **new** plans going forward.
